Its reference angular velocity is $$\boxed{
\omega_0=\frac{2\pi}{\mathrm{Tick}_0}.
}$$

Therefore $$f=\frac{f_0}{n},
\qquad
\boxed{
\omega=\frac{\omega_0}{n}.
}$$

During one zero-frame Tick, the angular progress is $$\boxed{
\Delta\theta_{\mathrm{per\ Tick}_0}
=
\omega\,\mathrm{Tick}_0
=
\frac{2\pi}{n}.
}$$
